    <GaugingStation location="Fruid" name="Fruid Water" number="21001">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound sharp-edged weir. Flows affected by Fruid Reservoir and diverted to Talla Reservoir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Flows in excess of 15.8cumecs are truncated and have to be estimated (this is said to occur once or twice per year). Theoretical rating for weir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound sharp-edged weir (9m wide) about 3km above the confluence with the Tweed. Fruid Reservoir opened 1968 for public water supply after station closed.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Captures 1959 minimum that predates reservoir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">21.4 sq.km (90%) of catchment area controlled. Aqueduct diverts water to Talla Reservoir from 1954 onwards.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mainly Silurian rock and boulder clay. Peat on high ground. High moorland; rough pasture; tree cover.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">SP</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="The station is only at estimating flow up to a value just below the QMED. Therefore this QMED is slightly less reliable than most but does give an approximate estimate that may be useful." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Most POT above top of chart. Method of extrapolation not known." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
